hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2926","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir, narrated to us Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who narrated to me Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid and 'Ata', on the authority of Jabir ibn 'Abdullah (RA), who said:

The people began to talk a great deal, so we set out as pilgrims until there remained between us and the end of the ihram (ihram exit) only a few nights. Then someone said, ""We have been commanded to end our ihram."" So one of us would go to 'Arafah with his private parts dripping with semen. This reached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so he stood up to deliver a sermon and said:

""O people, do you inform me about Allah? By Allah, I know Allah better than you and I fear Him more than you. If I were to go back to the beginning of my affair, I would not have brought sacrificial animals with me, and I would have ended my ihram just as they have ended theirs. So whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him fast three days during the Hajj and seven when he returns to his family. And whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him slaughter it.""

We used to slaughter a camel on behalf of seven people.

**CHAPTER:**"
"2927","It was narrated from 'Aṭā' that Ibn 'Abbās (RA) said:
""On that day, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) distributed some sheep among his companions. Sa'd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (RA) received a ram, so he slaughtered it for himself. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stopped at 'Arafah, he commanded Rabī'ah ibn Ummayyah ibn Khalaf to stand beneath the udder of his she-camel. The Prophet (ﷺ) then said to him:
'Proclaim, O people! Do you know what month this is?'
They said: 'The sacred month.'
He said: 'Do you know what land this is?'
They said: 'The sacred land.'
He said: 'Do you know what day this is?'
They said: 'The day of the greatest Hajj.'
The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed, Allah has made your lives, your wealth, and your honor as sacred to you as this month of yours, this land of yours, and this day of yours.'
Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) completed his Hajj. When he stopped at 'Arafah, he said: 'This is the standing place; all of 'Arafah is a standing place.'
And when he stopped at Muzdalifah, he said: 'This is the standing place; all of Muzdalifah is a standing place.'""

**CHAPTER:**"
